# White Ward gives Bot2's Savannah Lions protection from white (CR 702.16). On turn 3 Bot1 cannot target the Lions with
# Holy Strength, a white Aura spell (CR 702.16b; the refusal, and Bot1 has the mana to spare), and Bot1's Savannah Lions
# attacking into it is blocked by the other Lions: the attacker's damage is white and prevented (CR 702.16e), so Bot2's
# 2/1 Lions survives with no damage marked (without White Ward it would die) while Bot1's Lions dies. White Ward is
# white itself, yet stays on the Lions (CR 702.16n).

